      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. but what about the downsides though? like, did unions ever actually hurt the economy or make things worse for people who weren't in them?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, unions did have some downsides. Critics argue that strong union presence can lead to higher labor costs, which may affect businesses' competitiveness and potentially result in job losses or reduced investments. Additionally, unions have occasionally faced allegations of corruption, mismanagement, or being exclusionary in nature, which could harm their reputation and effectiveness. When unions exert too much power, it can also lead to overregulation or bureaucratic inefficiencies in some industries. Moreover, not everyone benefits from union membership since it often only encompasses a portion of the workforce, leaving some workers without its protections. Overall, while unions greatly contributed to the growth of the middle class and bolstered democratic engagement, there were complex economic and social trade-offs involved.",
